codex
Two design gaps remain. The plan can still skip evidence of prior article use, and its 72-hour rule changes D431’s release condition without a recorded decision that replaces it. [Run plan §1.2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v7.md:59) · [Run plan §1.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v7.md:165) · [D431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4800)

- **Loss with an undersized subgroup — resolved.** An undersized subgroup blocks a lead. A loss established by the paired counts or another guardrail still stands. [Run plan §1.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v7.md:149) · [Verdict rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v7.md:175)
- **Same-day eligibility — still open.** v7 specifies concurrent launches, a 72-hour window, and a diagnostic result if timing fails. D665 changed only D431’s frozen-reference requirement. Record an explicit decision replacing the calendar-day requirement for this run before any paid send, or keep D431’s rule. [Run plan §1.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v7.md:167) · [Calendar-day definition](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/WIRING-DESIGN.md:9) · [D665](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9428)
- **Whole-file exemption — still open.** Line 62 says to scan other tables in the same file. Line 68 still excludes source copies from the search. Remove the file-level exception. [Run plan §1.2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v7.md:59)
- **Earlier corpus builds — resolved, with a new gap.** Removing the 90% threshold fixes the treatment of older builds. But a probe’s selected articles can use the same columns. Freeze the exemption for tables documented as corpus storage and keep probe or fixture use in the census even when the columns match. [Run plan §1.2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v7.md:50) · [D665](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9411)
- **Mapping splits — resolved.** The two countings now specify which system gets the benefit of a disputed match. [Run plan §1.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v7.md:122) · [Counting rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v7.md:142)

NOT READY: settle D431’s timing rule explicitly and exempt only documented corpus storage while scanning every other table.
